The most recent version of the BMW 335d is from the F30 generation, produced until 2019 [2]. It was replaced by the M340d in the current G20 generation [Search results confirm M340d in G20, 335d not listed]. Therefore, I will evaluate the F30 BMW 335d, focusing on the later model years (post-facelift 2015-2019) where applicable.

Here is the evaluation of the F30 BMW 335d based on the provided scoring guide and search results:

-   **price_usd**: The F30 335d is a used car. Used prices in the UK market are typically in the £10,000 - £20,000+ range [Search results for used prices]. Converting this to USD (~$12,500 - $25,000+) places it well below the average new car price of $35,000, scoring positively.
-   **total_cost_estimate_5yr_usd**: As a performance-oriented premium diesel, the 335d will have higher than average costs for maintenance and potential repairs, especially as it ages [26]. While the purchase price is lower, the 5-year cost of ownership will likely exceed the $40,000 average for a new car. Scores negatively.
-   **insurance_usd_yr**: The 335d is a powerful diesel BMW with xDrive, placing it in higher insurance groups [Search needed for specific 335d UK insurance group, defaulting to negative based on general powerful BMW trend]. Scores negatively.
-   **maint_usd_yr**: BMW maintenance costs are generally higher than average [26]. Scores negatively.
-   **repair_risk_score**: The N57 diesel engine is generally considered reliable, but like any complex modern diesel, components like the DPF and EGR can require attention, especially if not driven on longer journeys [26]. Reliability is decent but not top-tier. Scores slightly negatively.
-   **hp**: The F30 335d produces 313 hp [7, 8, 9, 13, 17, 21, 26, 37]. This is significantly above the market average of 200 hp. Scores highly positively.
-   **torque**: The F30 335d produces 630 Nm (465 lb-ft) of torque [7, 8, 9, 13, 21, 26, 37]. This is substantially above the market average of 190 lb-ft. Scores highly positively.
-   **cylinder_count**: It features a 6-cylinder inline engine [9, 13, 17, 21]. While 4-cylinders are common, 6-cylinders are still prevalent in this segment and offer performance benefits. Around average.
-   **engine_displacement**: The engine is 3.0L (2993 cm³) [7, 8, 9, 13, 21]. This is around the market average for engine displacement today, especially considering it's a powerful turbocharged diesel. Around average.
-   **accel_0_60_sec**: 0-60 mph is around 4.6-4.8 seconds [19, 21, 26]. This is significantly faster than the market average of 7.5 seconds. Scores highly positively.
-   **top_speed**: Top speed is electronically limited to 155 mph (250 km/h) [7, 8, 9, 13, 21]. This is around the market average of 150 mph. Around average.
-   **drive_type**: Primarily All-Wheel Drive (xDrive) for the 335d [7, 8, 9, 13, 17, 21, 26, 37]. AWD is the market average.
-   **transmission_type**: Equipped with an 8-speed automatic (Steptronic) transmission [7, 8, 13, 17, 21, 26]. This is the most common and highly-rated type. Scores positively.
-   **offroad_ability**: This is a sedan/touring car, not designed for off-road use. Scores poorly.
-   **braking_dist_ft**: BMWs are known for strong braking performance. M Sport brakes were often fitted or optional [20, 24]. While specific distance wasn't found, it's expected to be better than average. Scores positively.
-   **size**: The F30 sedan length is around 4624-4633 mm (182.0-182.4 inches) [2, 7, 8, 10, 13, 15, 27, 35]. This is around the average for a modern sedan (~4600mm). Around average.
-   **wheelbase**: Wheelbase is 2810 mm (110.6 inches) [2, 7, 8, 10, 13, 15, 27, 38, 46]. This is slightly above the average for a modern car (~2700mm). Scores slightly positively.
-   **body_style**: Primarily 4-door Sedan (Saloon), also available as a 5-door Touring (Estate) [2, 17, 29, 35]. Sedan is the market average.
-   **seats**: Typically 5 seats [Search needed for F30 335d seats, defaulting to 5 based on 3 Series standard]. This is the market average.
-   **cargo_space**: Cargo space is 480 L (16.95 cu ft or 17 cu ft) for the sedan [8, 10, 14, 24, 25, 35, 43]. This is around the market average (~15 cu ft). Scores slightly positively.
-   **rear_space**: Rear legroom in the F30 was improved over the E90 but still not class-leading compared to larger sedans [14, 25, 35, 38]. Scores around average.
-   **ground_clearance_in**: Ground clearance is around 140-145 mm (5.5-5.7 inches) [8, 10, 13, 31, 38, 46]. This is typical for a sedan but below the average for compact crossovers (~6.5"). Scores negatively. xDrive models might sit slightly higher than sDrive [24, 28, 31].
-   **turn_radius_ft**: Turn radius is around 11.3-11.7 m (37.1-38.4 ft) [4, 8, 12, 23, 32, 39, 46]. This is around the market average (~36 ft). Around average or slightly negative.
-   **mpg**: Fuel economy for the diesel is rated highly, with combined figures around 45-50+ US mpg (50-60+ UK mpg) in real-world driving [5, 26, 36, 47]. Official figures were higher [44]. This is significantly above the market average (~30 mpg). Scores highly positively.
-   **co2_g_km**: CO2 emissions are relatively low for a non-electric vehicle, around 143 g/km [13]. This is well below the average for a non-hybrid gasoline car (~175 g/km). Scores positively.
-   **electric_range_mi**: Not a battery electric vehicle. Scores -1.00.
-   **charge_speed_kw**: Not a battery electric vehicle. Scores -1.00.
-   **style_sleek_vs_boxy**: The F30 has a conventional sedan shape, neither particularly sleek nor boxy [14]. Around average.
-   **style_aggression_rating**: The F30 has a sporty design, especially with M Sport packages [20, 24, 38, 45]. Scores slightly positively. The 335d is described as a "sleeper" due to its understated looks relative to performance [5, 24].
-   **style_modernity_rating**: The F30 design is from the 2010s and looks somewhat dated compared to the latest models [25]. Scores negatively.
-   **handling_rating**: The BMW 3 Series is known for excellent handling and driving dynamics [4, 24, 28, 33, 34]. Scores highly. Some reviewers noted the electronic steering had less feel than older hydraulic systems [24, 34]. Standard SE suspension on the 335d could have more body roll than desired, but M Sport suspension or aftermarket options improve this [34]. Averaging to highly positive.
-   **ride_comfort_rating**: Ride is described as a good balance between sportiness and comfort, though M Sport suspension can be firm [28, 33]. Standard SE suspension on the 335d is comfortable but can be crashy over bumps [34]. Scores around average or slightly above depending on suspension. Averaging to slightly above average.
-   **cabin_noise_rating**: Cabin noise is generally well-controlled [5, 33]. Scores above average.
-   **shift_smooth_rating**: The 8-speed automatic transmission is widely praised for its smooth and responsive shifts [5, 28]. Scores highly positively.
-   **steering_feel_rating**: Steering is typically well-weighted and direct, though some reviewers noted a reduction in feel compared to older generations [24, 34]. Still scores positively.
-   **adas_score**: The F30 offered some ADAS features (like adaptive cruise control, parking sensors, collision warning, lane assist) [4, 24], but not the extensive suites found in the latest vehicles. Scores around average for its time, but below average compared to today's best.
-   **visibility_rating**: Visibility is generally considered good [Search needed for specific F30 visibility reviews, defaulting to average].
-   **headlight_rating**: Available with Halogen, Xenon, or LED headlights [24, 43]. Halogens are poor, Xenons are below average, LEDs are around average compared to modern standards. Scores around average or slightly below depending on the specific headlights fitted.
-   **security_rating**: Standard security features for a premium car of its era (alarm, immobilizer, tracking systems via connected services were optional). Scores positively.
-   **screen_in**: Available iDrive screen sizes varied, with larger screens available [20, 25]. An 8.8-inch screen was common with Professional Navigation [20]. This is around average compared to modern screens.
-   **infotainment_ux_rating**: The iDrive system in the F30 was improved over previous generations and generally considered good, though perhaps not as intuitive as the very best modern systems [25, 35]. Scores above average for its time, but around average compared to today.
-   **smartphone_connect_rating**: Bluetooth for calls and audio streaming was standard [Search needed for F30 Bluetooth]. USB input was available [5]. Apple CarPlay was introduced later in the F30's life, often as an option [24]. Lacks the seamless wireless integration of the latest systems. Scores around average or slightly below compared to today.
-   **audio_rating**: Standard audio system was likely average, with optional upgraded systems (like Harman Kardon) available [20, 24]. Scores around average for the standard system.
-   **usb_ports**: Had USB socket [5]. Likely 1 or 2 ports standard. Below average compared to modern cars with multiple ports.
-   **comfort_feature_score**: Offers a good range of comfort features, including heated seats, power seats, dual-zone climate control, leather upholstery [20, 24]. Scores above average for the general market.
-   **convenience_feature_score**: Available features included parking sensors, keyless ignition (Comfort Access optional), reversing camera [20, 24]. Lacks some of the advanced convenience features of the latest cars (360 cameras, advanced parking). Scores above average for its time, but around average compared to today.
-   **brand_prestige_rating**: BMW is a premium brand. Scores highly.
-   **model_prestige_rating**: The 3 Series is a core, well-regarded model in the BMW lineup. Middle of the range for the brand.
-   **trim_prestige_rating**: The 335d was a high-performance diesel trim, positioned below the M3 [26, 35]. Scores negatively as a top trim within the diesel range.
-   **interior_luxury_rating**: Interior materials and build quality were high, offering a premium feel for its time [4, 25, 38]. Scores positively.
-   **interior_tech_focus_rating**: The F30 interior has a mix of physical controls and a screen. It's not as screen-dominated as the latest interiors [38]. Scores around average compared to modern tech focus.

